From a8c3ff7ea607cc67485188ca7c980d0734431244 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:49:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] alarmtimer: honour the wakeup setting of the alarmtimer
 device

With wakeup disabled through sysfs (alarmtimer.N.auto/power/wakeup),
alarm timers neither arm the RTC nor abort a suspend; they fire once
something else wakes the system. A sleep policy can then keep the
alarms of a container (Droidloom's Android) from waking the phone while
it is offline, and set the RTC itself for alarm clocks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel/time/alarmtimer.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c b/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c
index ea5be5870e51..acd6bc99112e 100644
--- a/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c
+++ b/kernel/time/alarmtimer.c
@@ -234,6 +234,14 @@ static int alarmtimer_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	if (!rtc)
 		return 0;
 
+	/*
+	 * Wakeup disabled through sysfs: alarm timers neither arm the RTC
+	 * nor abort the suspend. They fire once the system is woken by
+	 * something else.
+	 */
+	if (!device_may_wakeup(dev))
+		return 0;
+
 	/* Find the soonest timer to expire */
 	for (i = 0; i < ALARM_NUMTYPE; i++) {
 		struct alarm_base *base = &alarm_bases[i];
-- 
2.56.1

